- op: discuss  # 5294
  at: '2026-08-22T20:20:41Z'  # 5294
  by: agent  # 5294
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5294
  clock: 4  # 5294
  nonce: '5294'  # 5294
  message: "PANEL RESIDUE — evidence that existed only in conversation, recorded before\ncompaction. NONE of this was re-verified by me; it is attributed to the judge\nthat produced it and labelled accordingly. Treat it as leads, not findings.\n\n*** (1) THE FIX MUST NOT BE KEYED TO PARAMETER SYNTAX. *** The refuter judge\nbuilt fixtures showing a bare `confirmed` with NO caveat for receivers that are\nnone of \"an unannotated parameter\":\n    dict-subscript receiver          upload(ctx[\"client\"], ...)\n    **kwargs\n    a module global\n    an in-repo factory return\n    self.<attr>                      (this item)\n    AND a function that DOES have an in-repo caller, where the argument passed\n    is itself untypable -- so \"zero in-repo callers\" is not the extension of\n    \"no type available\"\nAnything keyed to receiver SYNTAX will ship a disclosure whose extension does\nnot match its sentence. Key on the proposition instead: THIS RECEIVER'S TYPE IS\nUNKNOWN.\n\n*** (2) A REAL CLEAN VERDICT WHERE THE SHIPPED CAVEAT UNDER-REPORTS ITSELF. ***\nStronger than this item's synthetic fixture, because it is on real code and the\nverdict is genuinely clean. Judge 2, qemu/scripts/qapi, B-net-send =\nconfirmed_with_caveats: the caveat lists 8 write() sites INCLUDING gen.py:336,\nwhile gen.py:247 self._genc.write() and gen.py:248 self._genh.write() are\nABSENT -- same file, adjacent lines, disclosed if the receiver is a local Name,\ninvisible if it is self.<__init__ field>. So the caveat reads as authoritative\nwhile silently under-counting its own site list. Honest scope, per that judge:\nthere the I/O is reachable via the in-repo QAPIGen.write, so this demonstrates\nunder-DISCLOSURE, not a missed boundary. WORTH RE-VERIFYING FIRST -- if it\nholds it is a better acceptance repro than the fixture on this item.\n\n*** (3) DENOMINATOR for \"bare confirmed is rare today\". *** Judge 1 swept 90\nreal leaf Python packages with a net_send must_not_exist claim: 82 inconclusive,\n3 violated, 3 confirmed (all trivial Django test fixtures), 2 errors, and ZERO\ncaveats of any kind. That is the number behind the anti-correlation argument --\nhonesty is currently carried by the uncovered-module gate, not by the caveats.\n\n*** (4) CORPUS SIZE for this item's shape. *** Judge 2: strict form\nself.<__init__ field> -- mitmproxy 114, meson 18, pretix 8, httpx 2\n(self.file.read()); loose form 4,773 production sites across 73 repos. Judge 1:\ndjango/django alone has 1,785 self.<attr>.<method>() sites.\n\n*** (5) ADJACENT, UNVERIFIED, POSSIBLY A SEPARATE DEFECT. *** Judge 2 observed\npants/.../util_rules returning `inconclusive` citing ONLY opaque launches, and\nnotes ADR-0016 section 4 says that case should be `confirmed_with_caveats`. I\ndid NOT reproduce this and it is NOT filed as an item -- filing on an\nunverified third-hand observation would be worse than recording it here. If it\nreproduces it is its own invariant.\n\n*** (6) FOR INV-fibis's half, not this one: *** Judge 1 found real production\nuntyped-parameter receiver sites in volume -- airflow session.execute()\n(taskinstance.py:993, dagrun.py:850, connection.py:640, variable.py:538),\nlitellm client.post() (anthropic/chat/handler.py:445,\nsagemaker/completion/handler.py:370), mlflow sftp.put(), feast conn.execute().\nThat population is real; what my measurement got wrong was the FRAME, not the\nexistence."  # 5294
