- op: discuss  # d3df
  at: '2026-08-22T22:13:36Z'  # d3df
  by: agent  # d3df
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d3df
  clock: 6  # d3df
  nonce: d3df  # d3df
  message: "FIXED AND VERIFIED ON THE MERGED TREE (dev 96561cf0f4, PR #480). Behavioral\nevidence, not a proxy: this item's own filed repro re-run at HEAD with fresh\nper-arm caches.\n\n    fx_A  self.sock = sock IN __init__       BEFORE: confirmed / \"No net_send\n                                                     chains found.\" / rc 0\n                                             AFTER:  confirmed_with_caveats,\n                                                     CAVEAT names app.py:9\n                                                     sendall()\n    fx_B  self.sock = sock in attach()       UNCHANGED in both arms\n    CONTROL-FSREAD                           violated / 2 chains in BOTH arms,\n                                             both directions -- the run worked\n\nThe two arms now AGREE, which is the point: the verdict no longer depends on\nWHERE the field was assigned.\n\nACCEPTANCE 2, django. db/backends/utils.py goes 0 of 10 -> 10 of 10\nself.<attr>.<method>() sites carrying an edge that names the method, including\nself.cursor.execute() at 103 and 105, executemany() at 114 and callproc() at\n71/73/76. NOTE ON THE FILED NUMBER: this item says 9 of 10 pre-fix; I measure\n0 of 10. The item's own text flags why -- the filer's index was a union across\nfiles, which biases TOWARD finding a match. Scoping to edges whose src IS that\nfile is the stricter frame. The direction and the conclusion are unchanged.\n\nTHE FIX IS ROUTE (b), AS THE ITEM ADVISED. The guards now gate the STAMP, not\nthe EMIT: an own field takes the same placeholder edge WITHOUT\ninherited_field_receiver. Route (a) was not taken. Every pre-existing shadow-FP\nlock passes unchanged, and the reason is structural rather than lucky: each of\nthem asserts the absence of the STAMP (or of a resolved ast_call_inherited_field\nedge), never the absence of an EDGE. test_self_field_untyped_own_field_no_hint\nwas passing VACUOUSLY -- there was no edge to carry a stamp -- and is now\nnon-vacuous.\n\nA/B IN BOTH SIGNS, arms differing in exactly this hunk, per-arm XDG_CACHE_HOME,\narm-took proven by marker presence/absence and the restore asserted by sha256:\n\n    django/db + mitmproxy + meson + httpx\n      +1,370 call edges, 0 relationships lost, 0 new edges stamped,\n      0 minted resolved\n      resolved_total +8, ALL from method-call-recovery-linker at conf 0.40.\n      Two spot-checked against source are TRUE POSITIVES: mitmproxy\n      self.addons is a DOTTED-constructor field (addonmanager.AddonManager(self))\n      that Case 2f cannot type, and meson self.whitespaces is genuinely a\n      WhitespaceNode.\n      ast_call_inherited_field UNCHANGED: 0 / 7 / 11 / 0 in BOTH arms.\n\nTHE ONE LOSS, STATED RATHER THAN NETTED OUT. 5 stamped edges vanish (django/db 2,\nmeson 3). Mechanism, read in code rather than guessed: edge_key is\n(src, dst, edge_type) and DELIBERATELY line-insensitive, and dedupe_edges keeps\nthe FIRST edge per key -- so a new own-field edge at an earlier line collapses\nwith a stamped edge to the same target and wins on encounter order. Worked\nexample: FieldFile.open, models/fields/files.py -- arm A had the line-83\nself.file.open() edge stamped inherited_field_receiver='file'; arm B has the\nline-81 self.storage.open() edge unstamped, with call_lines [81, 83]. It costs\nNO resolved output (ast_call_inherited_field is unchanged above) and the\ncollapsed site is preserved, not discarded. I also record that my first differ\nkeyed on meta.line -- which does not exist, line is TOP-LEVEL -- so its\n\"0 lost\" was a weaker claim than it read as; the corrected key found the losses.\n\nWHAT THIS DID NOT MOVE, WITH THE DENOMINATOR. 11 real scopes x 4 boundary claims\n= 44 verdict pairs (poetry installation/utils/mixology/puzzle/plugins/publishing/\nrepositories/inspection/console, httpx, django/db): ZERO verdicts moved. The\nreason is NOT that the fix is inert -- arm A produced NO bare `confirmed`\nANYWHERE in that population; every verdict was inconclusive (the uncovered-module\ngate firing first) or violated. That is this item's own anti-correlation\nargument showing up in data. So verdict-level movement is demonstrated on the\nISOLATING FIXTURE, NOT on real code, and I am not claiming otherwise.\n\nNOT COVERED BY THIS FIX, so the next reader does not assume it is. The shared\nSite-3 guards still route away an annotated `def m(self: T)` and a\n@staticmethod, so an own-field call in those shapes still emits nothing. And the\nother untypable-receiver shapes from the panel residue -- dict-subscript\nreceiver, **kwargs, module global, in-repo factory return -- are NOT this\nmechanism and are untouched here."  # d3df
